{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ZEP",
  "chapter": 2,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ZEP.2.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.2.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Assemble yourselves, yes, assemble, O nation not desired;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.2.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.2.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Before the decree bringeth forth, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "before",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the day passeth as the chaff, before the fierce anger of the LORD cometh upon you, before the day of the LORD'S anger cometh upon you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.2.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.2.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Seek ye the LORD, all ye meek of the earth, who have performed his judgment; seek righteousness, seek meekness: it may be ye will be hid in the day of the LORD'S anger.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.2.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.2.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For Gaza shall be forsaken, and Ashkelon a desolation: they shall drive out Ashdod at the noon day, and Ekron shall be rooted up.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.2.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.2.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Woe to the inhabitants of the sea coasts, the nation of the Cherethites! the word of the LORD ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " against you; O Canaan, the land of the Philistines, I will even destroy thee, that there shall be no inhabitant.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.2.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.2.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the sea coast shall be dwellings ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " cottages for shepherds, and folds for flocks.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.2.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.2.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the coasts shall be for the remnant of the house of Judah; they shall feed upon them: in the houses of Ashkelon shall they lie down in the evening: for the LORD their God will visit them, and turn away their captivity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.2.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.2.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have heard the reproach of Moab, and the revilings of the children of Ammon, by which they have reproached my people, and magnified ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "themselves",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " against their border.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.2.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.2.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I live, saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, Surely Moab shall be as Sodom, and the children of Ammon as Gomorrah, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the breeding of nettles, and salt-pits, and a perpetual desolation: the residue of my people shall lay them waste, and the remnant of my people shall possess them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.2.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.2.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This shall they have for their pride, because they have reproached and magnified ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "themselves",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " against the people of the LORD of hosts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.2.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.2.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The LORD ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "will be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " terrible to them: for he will famish all the gods of the earth; and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall worship him, every one from his place, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " all the isles of the heathen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.2.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.2.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ye Cushites also, ye ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " slain by my sword.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.2.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.2.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he will stretch out his hand against the north, and destroy Assyria; and will make Nineveh a desolation, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " dry like a wilderness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.2.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.2.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And flocks shall lie down in the midst of her, all the beasts of the nations: both the cormorant and the bittern shall lodge in the upper lintels of it; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " voice shall sing in the windows; desolation ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the threshholds: for he shall uncover the cedar work.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.2.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.2.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the rejoicing city that dwelt in security, that said in her heart, I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " none besides me: how is she become a desolation, a place for beasts to lie down in! every one that passeth by her shall hiss, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wag his hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
